WEBVTT

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:15.900
This barbecue is great!

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.440
Gammon, it's ready.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:18.450
Thanks.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.450
There's lots left, so eat up.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:25.720
I don't get it!

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.350
I just don't get it!

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:32.910
We're inside a Puzzle of
Fools right now, right?

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:35.820
That's right. What don't you understand?

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.930
Why you'd have a barbecue inside
a Puzzle of Fools?!

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:42.140
You can't tackle a challenge
on an empty stomach.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:46.030
Why not bread? Why not candy?
Why barbecue?!

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:48.900
You guys sure are flippant
for being in a deadly puzzle!

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.860
Nonoha, the meat's about ready.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:54.200
How 'bout you, Kaito? Give up?

00:00:55.490 --> 00:01:00.570
Line up eight skewers of barbecue,
four horizontal, four vertical.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:03.710
If any of the pieces overlap, you lose.

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:08.820
And don't move any of the meat
on their skewers.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:11.300
I heard you before, so shut up!

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.670
I'm just waitin' for the meat to cook.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:16.910
Okay, got it!

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:19.930
No playing with your food! No puzzles!

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:21.310
Say, Kaito...

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:26.520
Try moving one bone to solve
the mathematical formula.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.060
Cube, don't copy them!

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:30.810
It's a standing sausage puzzle!

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:33.570
Are you all idiots?

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:36.620
Is "genius" a euphemism for "idiot"?!

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:40.370
Now, calm down.
Our battle with the POG is over.

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:43.960
Let's just relax, have fun
and solve Puzzles of Fools.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:45.950
It's not relaxing or fun at all!

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:49.650
What're you so uptight about, Nonoha?

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:51.340
You've been a pain since this morning.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.380
Bastards!

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:56.610
It's a trap!
Don't step here (Especially YOU, Nonoha!)

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:58.010
Huh?

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:08.130
Are you an idiot?

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:10.050
Don't go running around
inside a Puzzle of Fools!

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:12.180
I don't want some idiot
saying I'm an idiot!

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:13.590
And I don't want some idiot saying,

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:15.900
"I don't want some idiot saying I'm an idiot!"

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:42.860
Lost

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:45.970
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.910
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:51.780
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:55.150
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:56.880
Found

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:01.070
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:05.580
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.390
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:11.510
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:14.840
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.720
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.440
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:20.810
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:23.010
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:25.410
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:28.850
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.570
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:32.380
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:35.240
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.390
It's now or never

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:38.510
That is what they say

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.570
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:44.240
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.410
That is what they say

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.570
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:51.070
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:52.300
That is what they say

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.710
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:03:57.110 --> 00:04:01.010
Orpheus Order

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:03.640
Is that so?

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:07.510
Understood. Please take care
on your way back.

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:15.340
That was Jikukawa.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:19.600
Kaito and the others
have released another Puzzle of Fools.

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:22.630
I'm grateful to them.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:26.960
As a POG seeking to mend mistaken ways
and make a fresh start.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.330
It's all over.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.950
Our days are tranquil once again.

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:36.900
Now, if only your memory would return.

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:40.460
Jin...

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:44.090
Let's have a leisurely
night of chess tonight.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:53.210
I still don't get it.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:54.480
What's that?

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:58.330
The reason you're still
tackling Puzzles of Fools.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:00.550
It's not just because you pledged

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:03.070
to "destroy all deadly puzzles," right?

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:05.340
I made a promise to Jin.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.780
That I would solve every
puzzle I came across.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:09.650
I gotta keep my promise.

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:11.950
Huh. Is that so?

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:15.740
Kaito, you didn't keep your
promise to ME, did you?

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:16.750
You remember?

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.800
I remember.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.600
When we went to Orpheus Island.

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:24.260
I'm sorry.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:28.790
No, come on, don't take it so seriously!

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:30.940
It's not that big a deal.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:32.980
I just threw it out there.

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:34.800
It IS a big deal.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:36.390
Kaito?

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:39.500
Even back then...

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:42.580
That day, the last day I saw Rook...

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:47.110
I was absorbed in a solving a puzzle
I'd almost finished,

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:50.120
and was later than I'd promised I'd be.

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:53.850
Because of that, we got
back later than usual,

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:57.460
and when those guys
realized Rook was gone, they...

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:03.590
If I'd just kept my promise...

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:06.270
Kaito.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.730
That's in the past.

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:12.620
Rook and the POG are back to normal.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.270
It's all in the past. Right?

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:19.660
Yeah.

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:37.410
Mama. It's about to begin.

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:41.090
Tomorrow, I will play with Kaito.

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:45.510
I look forward to it, Mama.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.410
Jeez, this traffic is terrible.

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:03.510
The students and teachers
are sure to be late, huh?

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.150
Was there an accident or something?

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:07.970
What a shock.

00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:11.340
I've never once
been late or absent for class...

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:13.700
I'm a failure as student
council vice president.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:16.130
It ain't that bad.

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:17.660
I do it all the time!

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:19.900
Do not compare me to YOU!

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:25.090
I may lose the trust of the
student council president.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:28.460
Upperclassman Jikukawa wouldn't
get angry about being late.

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:32.120
Yes, but still, personally...

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:35.390
A text?

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:37.930
Yeah. It's from Upperclassman Jikukawa.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:44.790
Ah, Kaito!

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:46.150
Kaito!

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:47.780
Sorry for calling you here.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:51.230
Upperclassman. What's all this traffic?

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:52.200
What's THAT?

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:01.120
"Keep out." Why can't we go in?

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:12.690
Hey! Has the POG not
gone back to normal?!

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:13.640
Huh?

00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:16.390
No one else would pull a stunt like this!

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:18.270
What are they after?!

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:20.520
No. It's not us.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.160
You're the one who was invited.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:24.740
That's why I texted you.

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:25.900
"Invited"?

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:27.100
Chieno.

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:28.060
Yes?

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:30.810
I have a favor, something
only you can do.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.190
What is it?

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:35.050
Will you have the school buses U-turn

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:37.860
and tell the students to stay at home for now?

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:40.370
Myself, alone?

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:41.870
Sorry.

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:44.620
Understood.

00:08:58.120 --> 00:08:59.760
What will you do, Kaito?

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:03.430
Kaito!

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:05.140
Huh? What, what?

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:16.950
Kaito!

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:17.820
Kaito!

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:26.500
Gimme a break!

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:28.480
Kaito!

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:36.170
Wh-What is this?

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:37.720
A hidden message.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:40.700
When you line up the letters hidden
on this tape, it spells

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:42.970
"Kaito In."

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:45.640
Oh! This is the "invitation"?

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:48.430
Who did this?

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:50.900
What do they want with Kaito?

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:54.170
Even if we wanted to follow him,
with the bridge like this...

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:56.280
There's a way.

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:02.190
Ahh, jeez! I slept in.

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:04.290
Huh? That's...

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:08.790
Hey, where y'all goin' in such a hurry?

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:11.540
Gammon, you come, too!

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:13.710
Uh, o-okay!

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:18.350
I don't know who, but
someone's screwin' with me!

00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:20.260
I'm gonna find 'em and kick their ass!

00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:35.240
The heck is this?!

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:43.990
This big-ass thing showed up
on campus overnight?

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:55.130
Th-This... Could it be...?

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:04.890
What is that?

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:07.510
It may be a puzzle.

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:10.270
Yeah. And it looks like a dangerous one.

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:15.130
A puzzle? If it's not the POG,
then who made that thing?

00:11:15.130 --> 00:11:17.200
To find that out...

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:19.660
I'm worried about Kaito. Let's hurry!

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:20.400
Okay.

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:27.130
A hidden message using mirrors.

00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:29.750
This is a puzzle, no doubt about it!

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:34.630
This way of doin' things pisses me off.

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:37.710
I'll do it! I accept this challenge!

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:40.510
Puzzle time... Let's begin!

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:52.300
Where's the puzzle, then?!

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:00.400
The glass panes became walls!

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:03.760
Hey! What kind of puzzle is this?! Open-

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:10.520
The glass has been both
smoke and mirrors.

00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:12.100
Just what's going on?

00:12:15.010 --> 00:12:17.840
Welcome to the Puzzle of Judgment.

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:19.460
It's you!

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:22.130
I saw you yesterday in
the Puzzle of Fools!

00:12:22.710 --> 00:12:23.980
Who are you?

00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:25.470
What do you want with me?!

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:29.660
The puzzle shall manifest soon.

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:33.500
Yes, a deadly puzzle you hate so much.

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:38.000
This area will become a maze of

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:40.480
the same glass that now surrounds you.

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:43.860
Dammit!

00:12:45.340 --> 00:12:47.980
That star mark in the center is you.

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:49.620
There are four routes.

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:52.340
But there is only one right answer.

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:55.120
Choose the wrong one
and this area will collapse.

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:59.670
I will head for the exit
on the correct route,

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:02.280
so you should use the same route to escape.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:06.320
Your hint is my reflection in the mirror.

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:08.180
However, as you mentioned earlier,

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:12.470
this glass can become
both smoke and mirror.

00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:16.020
If you can't get out within
one minute after I do,

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:18.020
you will die.

00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:21.600
Gimme a damn break.

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:24.480
I ain't losing to some deadly puzzle!

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:26.660
I'll solve it.

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:29.160
I'll solve it and I'll kick your ass!

00:13:30.260 --> 00:13:31.660
Well, do your best.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:34.310
Let's play up!

00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:42.150
I will move three times,
one block at a time, toward the exit.

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:44.040
The instant you say the answer,

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:45.990
the glass around you will open.

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:50.010
But first, you'll have to find out
which way you're facing.

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:52.810
<i>Just mirrors are one thing, </i>

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:55.700
<i>but they can become
glass, become smoke...</i>

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:58.710
<i>I have to find the one
right answer from inside</i>

00:13:58.710 --> 00:14:01.290
a massive combination of mirrors and glass?<i></i>

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:05.030
<i>That's one hell of a challenge!</i>

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:16.520
What is this? Where's the president?

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:19.830
Tamaki Chieno likes Souji Jikukawa.

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:27.470
You seem troubled... Young Lady.

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:29.810
Who're you?!

00:14:29.810 --> 00:14:33.190
Still, he is absorbed with Kaito Daimon.

00:14:33.190 --> 00:14:35.540
He won't even look at you.

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:37.940
How sad, Miss Tamaki Chieno.

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:45.240
Kaito Daimon should just
disappear for good.

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:52.020
<i>Calm down. </i>

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:54.390
<i>First, I have to
sort this information...</i>

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:57.470
<i>The guy ain't in front of me.</i>

00:14:57.470 --> 00:15:00.330
<i>I see one of him to my
right, two to my left,</i>

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:04.280
<i>one at my rear right and three at my rear left.</i>

00:15:04.990 --> 00:15:06.510
<i>Gotta pare that down.</i>

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:09.280
<i>This maze is made up of squares and walls</i>

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:11.300
<i>that form diagonal lines between them.</i>

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:13.270
<i>So then, the angles of incidence and</i>

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:15.070
<i>reflection of light coming down the maze</i>

00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:16.660
<i>is 45 degrees each.</i>

00:15:17.130 --> 00:15:18.740
<i>Together, 90 degrees.</i>

00:15:18.740 --> 00:15:20.270
<i>It will move along right angles.</i>

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:23.590
<i>The maze can be approached linearly.</i>

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:30.810
<i>I can't get sidetracked by nonessentials.</i>

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:32.690
<i>I have to look only at what's</i>

00:15:32.690 --> 00:15:34.330
<i>right behind and right to the side of me.</i>

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:37.320
<i>Light reflected this way
on a 90-degree angle</i>

00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:39.830
<i>will come in from three directions.</i>

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:41.870
<i>If that guy can get to
the exit in three blocks,</i>

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:44.290
<i>it has to be at one of these four places.</i>

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:50.360
<i>If it's A, there's no way there'd be
three reflections of him.</i>

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:53.210
<i>So, A ain't the right answer.</i>

00:15:53.210 --> 00:15:54.260
<i>If B... It's possible.</i>

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:56.960
<i>And C... Possible.</i>

00:15:56.960 --> 00:16:00.810
<i>D... It's possible, too.</i>

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:05.940
Having a hard time, aren't you?

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:08.910
I'm disappointed, Phi-Brain.

00:16:08.910 --> 00:16:12.950
Rather, he who rejected
the Phi-Brain, Kaito Daimon.

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:14.940
How do you know that?!

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:17.550
I've watched this whole time.

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:19.080
The fight between you and your friend.

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:21.210
It was quite fun.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:22.990
It rivaled the match

00:16:22.990 --> 00:16:26.270
between Count Pythagoras and Jin Makata.

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:28.340
You know that, too?!

00:16:28.640 --> 00:16:30.400
Of course I do.

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:32.170
It was the one chance

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:34.220
to lay eyes on the Book of God.

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:36.140
Who the hell are-?!

00:16:37.110 --> 00:16:41.240
Kaito. You hate puzzles that harm others,

00:16:41.240 --> 00:16:42.900
but that is hypocrisy.

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:45.720
You yourself have harmed
many, haven't you?

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:46.690
What was that?!

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:50.470
Yes. You casually break promises,

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:52.990
think nothing of harming your friends.

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:03.320
You've always been alone,
haven't you? Kaito.

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:10.500
Those are all the hints that you get.

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:13.220
You can't see my last movement.

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:17.500
All right, show me you can escape
in your remaining minute.

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:26.870
I can't lose.

00:17:26.870 --> 00:17:31.440
I made a promise...
to solve all puzzles!

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:38.770
Kaito's brain is becoming active!

00:17:38.770 --> 00:17:39.780
Active?

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:44.660
It's just like when he wore
the Armlet of Orpheus!

00:17:45.590 --> 00:17:49.830
By analyzing what I can from light
shining around right angles,

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:52.360
I should be able to
figure out where he is.

00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:58.430
I could see in three directions at the start:
right, left and behind.

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:01.490
That ruled out Route A.

00:18:01.490 --> 00:18:06.930
At his next movement,
he appeared to my right and left.

00:18:06.930 --> 00:18:11.890
That makes B, C and D all possible.

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:16.850
The third time I saw him, he was
also to the right and left.

00:18:16.850 --> 00:18:20.750
Route B would make that possible.

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:22.740
C would be possible, too.

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:24.870
Route D is possible, too.

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:26.290
They all are.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:30.840
Which is it? Which of those three is it?

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:34.880
What's different? What is it?

00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:39.130
What's different about
these three routes?

00:18:39.830 --> 00:18:42.510
You've always been alone,
haven't you? Kaito.

00:18:43.380 --> 00:18:44.260
That's it!

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:46.060
The distance.

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:50.020
Last time I saw him,
he was five blocks ahead of me.

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:55.660
And on the opposite side,
he was three blocks ahead.

00:18:56.390 --> 00:18:59.530
If it were Route B, the
light that reached me

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:01.920
would be three and nine blocks ahead.

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:03.600
If it were Route D,

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:06.250
light would be from
11 and five blocks ahead.

00:19:06.730 --> 00:19:08.820
If it were Route C,

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:12.350
light would come from
three and five blocks ahead.

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:13.990
So...

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:18.420
The answer is, the way right
behind me, Route C!

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:42.570
Kaito!

00:19:45.390 --> 00:19:46.330
Kaito!

00:20:00.610 --> 00:20:02.030
That was close!

00:20:02.030 --> 00:20:03.430
By the skin of our teeth, eh?

00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:06.430
Kaito! Cube!

00:20:07.050 --> 00:20:08.260
You did it!

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:09.950
Think I lost
a couple of years off my life.

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:11.910
We came through the emergency-use rear

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:13.950
gates Upperclassman Jikukawa told us about.

00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:16.960
Sure enough, you're no good
without me, Kaito.

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:18.950
Why you...!

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:21.070
That was a close one, Kaito.

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:26.830
I applaud you for solving that
without the Armlet of Orpheus.

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:32.370
But... This is not enough
to be of use for our plans.

00:20:32.740 --> 00:20:34.300
Who the hell are you?!

00:20:35.780 --> 00:20:36.690
Kaito.

00:20:37.850 --> 00:20:40.540
You shall continue to
be betrayed by those

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:43.720
you trust as you are challenged by the Game.

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:45.050
What?!

00:20:45.050 --> 00:20:47.240
But you already know this.

00:20:48.190 --> 00:20:51.060
After all, it was YOU
who broke the promise.

00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:52.500
Promise?

00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:54.150
Answer the question!

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:56.440
This prank of yours cost a lot of money!

00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:58.360
Who the hell are you?!

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:02.270
The Orpheus Order.

00:21:03.090 --> 00:21:05.670
We embrace the great Orpheus,

00:21:05.670 --> 00:21:10.450
and seek to
free Man from the yoke of the lesser gods.

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:13.090
That's...!

00:21:13.090 --> 00:21:15.460
An Armlet of Orpheus! It can't be!

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:21.010
My name is Freecell. I
hold an Orpheus Ring,

00:21:21.010 --> 00:21:22.720
and am a Phi-Brain child.

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:25.720
That's not possible!

00:21:36.660 --> 00:21:37.670
Chieno!

00:21:37.670 --> 00:21:38.690
The vice president!

00:21:39.890 --> 00:21:41.930
Kaito Daimon.

00:21:41.930 --> 00:21:45.070
You will fight me. Via puzzles.

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:42.840
Eiyuukidori, itsudatte shinjita muteki no kankaku
Playing the hero, a sense of invincibility

00:22:42.840 --> 00:22:45.550
Eiyuukidori, itsudatte shinjita muteki no kankaku
You always believed in

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:51.390
Tatakatte iru no wa chikyuu no tame nanka ja nai
You're not fighting for the sake of the world or anything

00:22:51.390 --> 00:22:54.330
Motto maipeesu de
It's for a more leisurely

00:22:54.330 --> 00:22:59.230
Sou motto shoujiki na onegai no tame
Yeah, more straightforward request

00:22:59.690 --> 00:23:07.480
Nandotonaku kizutsuitemo tachiagare, hero
Even if you're wounded over and over, rise up, hero

00:23:07.480 --> 00:23:13.210
Kitto daijoubu, kimi o mamorunda
It's sure to be all right, I'll protect you

00:23:13.710 --> 00:23:17.040
Machigai da to shitemo tomarenai
Even if it's wrong, it can't be stopped

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:20.860
Seikai ka nante wakaranai
I don't know if it's the right answer

00:23:21.590 --> 00:23:24.640
Donna toki demo original ni, step o fumidashiteku
No matter the situation

00:23:24.640 --> 00:23:27.330
Donna toki demo original ni, step o fumidashiteku
I'll take those first steps, originally

00:23:27.330 --> 00:23:30.850
Dramatic ni, mawaru sekai de
On this spinning world, I'm searching, dramatically

00:23:30.850 --> 00:23:34.520
Kiwameita wonder sagashiteru
For wonders that sparkle

00:23:35.240 --> 00:23:38.570
Boku, shijou saikou no tabi o tsuzukeyou
Me, I'll keep going on the greatest journey in history

00:23:38.570 --> 00:23:41.090
Image shite shiawase na mirai e
To the happy future I imagined

00:23:41.090 --> 00:23:43.060
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:44.440 --> 00:23:46.010
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:47.850 --> 00:23:51.440
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:51.440 --> 00:23:52.870
(Mirai e)
(To the future)

00:24:02.920 --> 00:24:04.590
What's the vice president doing?!

00:24:04.590 --> 00:24:06.880
You seem troubled, Young Lady.

00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:08.400
They're here! The Orpheus Order!

00:24:08.400 --> 00:24:11.840
My name is Pinochle.
Shall I present you with

00:24:11.840 --> 00:24:13.580
a charm to win back the man of your heart?

00:24:13.580 --> 00:24:14.630
I don't need that!

00:24:14.630 --> 00:24:17.100
Don't underestimate a woman's love power!

00:24:17.100 --> 00:24:18.970
Oh, you're SO scary...

00:24:18.970 --> 00:24:21.100
Next time, "Darkness of the Heart"

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:22.730
Sorry to keep you all waiting!

00:24:21.620 --> 00:24:26.840
Darkness of the Heart

00:24:22.730 --> 00:24:26.130
Our school love drama is about to begin!
